commit 4e22cfa3a7b72f820eecede578b71733b5d996be
Author:     John Bieling <john@thunderbird.net>
AuthorDate: Wed Jan 29 08:11:14 2025 +0200
Commit:     John Bieling <john@thunderbird.net>
CommitDate: Wed Jan 29 08:11:14 2025 +0200

    Bug 1913621 - Allow extensions to control where links should be opened (in Thunderbird or in the user's default browser). r=aleca,mkmelin


    We fixed many of Thunderbird's link issues in Bug 1905616, and we can
    now offer to handle links by Thunderbird, even if they go to different
    hosts. This is for example needed for add-ons utilizing the spaces bar
    to load intranet pages, which might be spread across different domains.

    This does not mean that Thunderbird can now be used as a browser. We
    lack support of many web features and implementing those does not
    align with Thunderbird's overall strategy.

    This patch adds a `linkHandler` property to the create() functions of
    the tabs API, the windows API and the spaces API. The new property can
    be set to `balanced` (links to same host are opened in Thunderbird,
    everything else in the user's default browser), `strict` (only links to
    the same page are opened in Thunderbird) or `relaxed` (all links are
    opened in Thunderbird).

    Differential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D232068

